   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi folks,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using plotTangentSpace to warp my reference mesh to the extremes of the PC axes, but when I do the meshes come out completely black. I still see details but the surface is like tar. My original mesh has no color and I used the following code (please excuse the messy naming)</div><div><br></div><div><div>readland.nts(&quot;A_bakeri_c_USNM327157_83ldmks.nts&quot;)-&gt;Abaknts</div><div>Abaknts[,,1]</div><div>warpRefMesh(bakeri_c_ply, Abaknts[,,1], ref, color = NULL, centered = FALSE)</div></div><div><br></div><div>PCA_bs &lt;- plotTangentSpace(A_bs, warpgrids = TRUE, mesh = bakeri_c_ply)<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks if someone can help me to change the color to something more visible like gray.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Christy</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pgGawlToCgAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
