     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<span></span>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">chip...@unimelb.edu.au</a><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Monday, February 19, 2018 8:14 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] change warp mesh colour from black<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi folks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;m using plotTangentSpace to warp my reference mesh to the extremes of the PC axes, but when I do the meshes come out completely black. I still see details but the surface is like tar. My original mesh has no color and I used the following\r\n code (please excuse the messy naming)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">readland.nts(&quot;A_bakeri_c_USNM327157_83ldmks.nts&quot;)-&gt;Abaknts<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Abaknts[,,1]<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">warpRefMesh(bakeri_c_ply, Abaknts[,,1], ref, color = NULL, centered = FALSE)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">PCA_bs &lt;- plotTangentSpace(A_bs, warpgrids = TRUE, mesh = bakeri_c_ply)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks if someone can help me to change the color to something more visible like gray.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Best,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Christy<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
